  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user, I want to pick my accent colour from a few ready-made colours or fine-tune it on the hue slider, and see the result live before I leave the screen, so that I choose a colour I like and that stays readable.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Presets on the shipped hue slider** (operator 2026-10-28: « au choix clair / sombre et disons 10 accentuation … essaye de prendre le spectre »; decision 12: keep the continuous slider and add 10 preset dots, no navy, since a fixed-saturation hue cannot give navy). Proposed hues, to confirm with the operator: Rouge 0.00, Orange HFR 0.091 (`orange-hfr`), Jaune 0.14, Vert 0.33, Sarcelle 0.47, Cyan 0.50, Cyan HFR 0.53 (default, 190°), Bleu 0.60, Violet 0.74, Rose 0.92. A preset only moves the slider: the stored keys and their shape stay LOT-121's (`theme_day_color_action`, `theme_night_color_action`).\n- **Live preview**: a sample (list row with the accent glyph, a link, a toggle, a badge) in light and dark next to the slider, updated as it moves.\n- **Readable accent text** (decision 14, intentional difference from legacy): the raw tint stays for fills and toggles; text and glyphs drawn in the accent use a derived colour of the same hue that reaches 4.5:1 on the surface (LOT-122's spec leaves this to LOT-180: the night tint is 3.5:1 on black at 240°). Rule in `docs/THEMES.md` §3.\n- Scope kept from the split of LOT-122 (#213): LOT-121 keeps the slider and its tints, LOT-122 the dark styles.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: low · **M4** (operator 2026-11-07)\n- GAP ids: 145, 146. UXD: UXD-22. Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-180-accent.md`.\n\n### Legacy counterpart\n\n`HFRswift/Swift/AppSettingsView.swift:326-333` (`applyTintHue`: day S0.65 B1.0, night S0.70 B0.95) and `:439-445` (« Teinte d'accent » slider) @ 87fe0d1c. Presets, preview and the derived text colour are new.\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-122 (#213, done)\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] An optional evolution: with no preset touched, colours and stored values are exactly LOT-121's.\n- [ ] Tapping a preset writes both accents in the legacy shape; the slider still writes any hue.\n- [ ] Contrast test: the derived accent text ≥ 4.5:1 on every surface of light, dark Standard, Plus sombre and Noir OLED, for every preset and for 0…1 in 0.01 steps.\n- [ ] The spec has its \"Legacy counterpart\" and \"UX evolutions\" sections.\n- [ ] View logic in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing; each new test shown to fail without the change; `xcodebuild build test` green on iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0); UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency.\n- [ ] This PR moves the LOT-180 row of `docs/LOTS.md` out of the M5 table and regenerates `tooling/roadmap/lots.json` and `milestones.json` (operator 2026-11-07 comment).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, docs/THEMES.md §3, the LOT-121 and LOT-122 specs. Claim with `/claim <session-id>`; PR body `LOT-180`, `Closes #420`, `Refs #154`, `Claim: <session-id>`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
